// Jest Snapshot v1, https://jestjs.io/docs/snapshot-testing

exports[`git.pull.watch read health given: [case1] two clones, each on its own pr, one pr goes dark when: [t0] #1220 gets no reply past the note bound; #1221 reads fine then: get names the read fault on the row of #1220 alone 1`] = `
"🐢 heres the wave...

🐚 git.pull.watch get
   └─ daemon v<key> · live · pid <pid> · last tick <n>s ago
      ├─ home: <home>/.rhachet/storage/repo=ehmpathy/role=mechanic/skill=git.pull.watch/v=<key>/bin
      └─ watches
         ├─ ehmpathy/surf-demo#1220 → @:mechanic (root: <root:surf-demo>) · read fault 1 min: github unreachable: repos/ehmpathy/surf-demo/pulls/1220 (status: none) dial tcp: lookup api.github.com: no such host
         └─ ehmpathy/surf-demo#1221 → @:mechanic-b (root: <root:surf-demo>)

🥥 did you know?
   └─ a read fault holds the cursors of that pr; alerts resume at its next good read, within 1 min
      ├─ a pr with no good read for the idle ttl ends its watch, with a note that names its last fault
      └─ each fault line is in the daemon log: cat <home>/.rhachet/storage/repo=ehmpathy/role=mechanic/skill=git.pull.watch/v=<key>/daemon.log
"
`;

exports[`git.pull.watch read health given: [case1] two clones, each on its own pr, one pr goes dark when: [t2] #1221 answers 404 then: one note reaches the clone of #1221, with the rewatch 1`] = `
"🐢 bummer dude...

🐚 git.pull.watch — #1221 answers 404 to the seaturtle token (gone, or out of its reach); watch ended
   └─ rewatch: rhx git.pull.watch set --which 1221 --mode apply"
`;

exports[`git.pull.watch read health given: [case2] a pr that answers 404 to the grove token, the seaturtle token not granted when: [t0] the first due read then: the note names the grove token and puts the seaturtle unlock before the rewatch 1`] = `
"🐢 bummer dude...

🐚 git.pull.watch — #1230 answers 404 to the grove token (@all.prep.GITHUB_TOKEN); watch ended
   ├─ the pr may be gone, or out of the grove token's reach; the seaturtle token was not granted
   ├─ 1. unlock: rhx keyrack unlock --owner ehmpath --env prep --key EHMPATHY_SEATURTLE_GITHUB_TOKEN
   └─ 2. rewatch: rhx git.pull.watch set --which 1230 --mode apply"
`;

exports[`git.pull.watch read health given: [case3] a pr whose every read faults, from the first when: [t0] the watch is set and the idle ttl passes then: one idle note names the rewatch 1`] = `
